# dotctl waybar decorator - round (Powerline half circles)
# Substitutes the canonical pointed chevrons with their round equivalents.
#
# Format: each non-comment line is `FROM TO` as bare 4-digit hex codepoints
# (whitespace-separated). At apply time dotctl substitutes both the JSON
# escape form (\uFROM -> \uTO) and any literal glyph occurrences in
# config.jsonc.
#
# Hex codepoints - NOT literal glyphs - on purpose: Powerline glyphs live in
# the Private Use Area, render as nothing in most editors/terminals, and get
# silently dropped when files round-trip through text tooling. The canonical
# configs carry \uXXXX escapes for the same reason (see the rsep-pulse
# history: the glyph vanished in an edit and nobody could see it happen).

# U+E0B0 right chevron -> U+E0B4 right half-circle
e0b0 e0b4

# U+E0B2 left chevron -> U+E0B6 left half-circle
e0b2 e0b6
